# `const url = new URL(line); line += ..; url.searchParams.get("k0")`: a URL that is never made is made after all where a value has to be decoded, of the operands as they are written. A name of a text in a builder is bound to the builder again by then, which has grown: such a URL is made where it is written. A text that every iteration passes is in no builder.
